        "title": "The code does what the authoring contract says",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-enforcement",
          "nodeId": "authoring-contract-enforcement-goal"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/goal.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "body": "Every switch the contract calls built is read by the code at the path it names, with the default it states, and a value outside its listed values is corrected or ignored where it is read, not passed on. A switch nothing reads is built or taken out of the contract.",
        "status": "in-progress",
        "successMetrics": [
          "Every built switch has a reader at its stated path, with its stated default.",
          "Where a switch lists valid values or a range, the code that reads it ignores or corrects anything else.",
          "A switch that nothing reads is built, or removed from the contract and the panel.",
          "A test holds the contract to the code, so the next drift fails instead of going unseen."
        ],
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1792950744123,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        },
        "notes": "2026-10-27: the audit is finished and its fixes are made. Six unread switches removed (79 switches); the edge draw loop and the stroke stack handle animation and pulse; glow, gradient and strokes can be edited in the panel; the edge style normalizer drops values the contract rules out; ELK is handed only listed values; the lane gap range agrees; and tests/authoringContractEnforcement.test.js holds the contract to the code, so a switch nothing reads fails it. showLabel now works on every node with a title bar. Left: edge effects (in progress) and the per-type check of node text styles."
      }
    },
