        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "status": "done",
        "body": "The first half counted readers; this half read the code for the rest: node styles, view, membrane, port, layout, root handle, semantic level. Every built switch has a reader (a test now says so). The findings and fixes are recorded on the tasks.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1793157495259,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        },
        "notes": "2026-10-27: done. Read the rest of the contract against the code. Honoured and safe on a bad value: node.style.* (FixedNode spreads the whole style onto the frame, so every key applies as CSS and the browser ignores a bad one), settings.layout.mode (manual stops the auto-placing), defaultLayout (applies when changed), direction, serpentine and cycle fallback, root.handle, view.fit (anything but window is screen), view.scroll, semanticLevel (including badge), port.direction (an unknown one matches no connection), port.dataType (any string, compared as written). Found and fixed: edge style values outside the contract were carried into the drawing (12b5242b); ELK was handed unchecked algorithm, routing and port constraints (12b5242b). Not what the contract says: showLabel is read by content nodes only (the contract already says so; see the new task)."
      }
    },
