        "title": "Say what the edge data switches do: flow, direction, strength, intent",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-enforcement",
          "nodeId": "authoring-contract-enforcement-data-switches"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "status": "done",
        "body": "Stored at edge.data and read by nothing but the panel's \"has values\" check. If they are annotations, the contract says so in each effect; if something acts on them, that is a feature to build. Waits on the question.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1793157495259,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        },
        "notes": "2026-10-27: removed. Michael: edges should support animation and the like; the particular data keys do not matter. Flow, direction, strength and intent are out of the contract (79 switches). They were only ever a panel convenience that translated to style (flow to animation, strength to width, direction to arrowheads); that panel section was removed this morning with the Meaning section. The real properties are edge.style.animation, animationSpeed, glow, gradient and strokes."
      }
