        "title": "Make edgeLaneGapPx agree with itself",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-enforcement",
          "nodeId": "authoring-contract-enforcement-lane-gap"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "status": "done",
        "body": "The contract and the panel slider say 0-60; EdgeLayer.js clamps to 0-50, so 51-60 do nothing. useGraphModes.js also reuses the value as the grid gap of the fallback layout, with a floor of 80, which is a different thing. One range everywhere; the fallback gap gets its own setting or its own constant.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1793157495259,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        },
        "notes": "2026-10-27: done. EdgeLayer now clamps the lane gap to the contract's 0-60 (it was 0-50), and the fallback grid layout has its own constant, FALLBACK_LAYOUT_GAP (80), instead of borrowing the lane gap with a floor. 12b5242b."
      }
    },
