        "title": "Check the enum values where they are read",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-enforcement",
          "nodeId": "authoring-contract-enforcement-check-enums"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "status": "done",
        "body": "The ELK algorithm, edge routing (from the settings) and port constraints are handed to ELK as written; port.dataType and port.direction are accepted as written (dataType falls back to value only when empty). Each reader ignores or corrects a value outside the contract's list and uses the default.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1793157495259,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        },
        "notes": "2026-10-27: done. getElkSettings replaces an algorithm, edge routing or port constraint outside the contract's list, and a spacing outside its range, with the default or the nearest limit. The port enums needed no change: an unknown direction matches no connection and dataType is compared as written. Edge style route, arrow position, width and arrow size outside the contract are dropped by the normalizer. 12b5242b."
      }
