      "data": {
        "title": "Edge animation and effects work end to end, and can be authored",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-enforcement",
          "nodeId": "authoring-contract-enforcement-edge-animation"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "status": "in-progress",
        "body": "Michael wants edges to support animation and the like, and thought there was territory here that was never built. There was. Done 2026-10-27: (1) the draw loop decided from the raw style whether to keep animating, so an animation written in any form but the plain word drew once and stood still (e9ef5bb9); (2) glow, gradient and stroke stacks could only be shown in the panel, and now have editors built from the contract's new fields (354f3fcd); (3) a stack of strokes ignored a pulse's width, and now takes it. Checked on a real canvas in the preview: flow, pulse, glow, dash, gradient and stroke stacks all draw, flow dots and the dash move, {type: \"flow\"} animates, a stack's thickness now oscillates under a pulse. Still open: only four animations exist (dash, glow, pulse, flow), so any other effect Michael has in mind is new; the panel's glow, gradient and stroke editors were rendered and tested but not yet used by hand in the editor (the edge Properties panel would not open from the preview); the passive workspace canvas is unchecked; a stroke's own dash and gradient are written by hand only.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1793158413840,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        },
        "notes": "2026-10-27: in progress; see the body for what is done and what is open."
      }
    },
