      "data": {
        "title": "Make showLabel work on every node type",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract-enforcement",
          "nodeId": "authoring-contract-enforcement-show-label"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "status": "done",
        "body": "The contract says it is partly built: only a content node's summary reads it, and other node types draw their label whatever it says. Decide which node types draw a label at all (a face or a glyph may not), then make the switch work on each of them or say on the switch which it applies to. Found in the audit; not fixed.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1793162214578,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        },
        "notes": "2026-10-27: done. A node's label is drawn in its title bar (a content node's summary also draws it). The bar now leaves the label text out when showLabel is false, through FixedNode, PortNode and NodeTypeBadge, and keeps the bar itself, since it is the drag handle and holds the actions; the label stays as the button's accessible name. Seen in the editor on an unknown-type node and a content node, with and without the switch. The contract's status is built. A graph tile's bar (a graph, not a node) is not a node switch and is unchanged."
      }
    },
    {
